do_1 = "In .github/workflows/wallet-test.yml:74-117 provide the native node prerequisites and pinned toolchains used by .github/workflows/node-build.yml:47-72, then invoke a Gateway test lifecycle script at services/wallet/gateway/test/support/run-paxeer-vitest.sh instead of the bare pnpm test command; preserve the frozen dependency installs, Anvil and PostgreSQL prerequisites and the full Gateway suite as the default invocation. The script starts the existing tools/qualification/localnode/v6120-node.sh with a unique environment file beneath its required lx-localnode directory, waits for its merge readiness checks at :57-80 and :788-806, sources LOCAL_NODE_RPC and LOCAL_NODE_HOME, exports HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL and EIP712_NODE_RPC_URL to that loopback endpoint, and runs pnpm test with any supplied focused arguments. Register cleanup before Vitest starts, stop only that disposable home with the fixture's --stop interface at :320 on success, failure or interruption, and preserve test failures and report cleanup failures. Keep the stream state empty and generated Gateway wallets unfunded, as services/wallet/gateway/test/agent-precompiles-streams.test.ts:283-327 and :353-357 require; use native handlers at 0x0906 and 0x0908, never Anvil replacements or public endpoints."
do_2 = "Extend tests/ci/test_wallet_js_suites_wired.py:47-57 to require the exact Gateway lifecycle-script command while retaining the exact pnpm test command for the other packages and every dependency, trigger and no-skipping assertion. Add test_gateway_vitest_paxeer_node_fixture to assert the workflow's node prerequisites precede its test step and execute that same lifecycle script against a real disposable node with the two existing EIP-712 cases at services/wallet/gateway/test/agent-precompiles-eip712.test.ts:269-310 and the two streams cases at services/wallet/gateway/test/agent-precompiles-streams.test.ts:334-387 selected explicitly. Assert exactly four passing cases with no skips, both URLs naming the ready loopback node, and the owned node processes stopped afterwards; cover cleanup after a failing focused invocation as well, without substituting RPC responses or altering either suite. Retain detailed output as private evidence and report any other Gateway failures separately without broadening the focused gate."
